# Task List
// A to-do list:  add a task, check it off, filter the list, and edit the selected tasks together.
// Its tasks are this project's own `<spell-view "task">`;  this file holds their list, and the app.
// Where they're kept is the person's pick, "Keep them in":  each place is a keeper in an API file of its own,
// TaskList.browser.api.spell, TaskList.server.api.spell, TaskList.csv.api.spell and TaskList.atmosphere.api.spell, all doing what TaskList.api.spell says.

## The checklist
// The tasks, each its own element inside it:  `<task-list-checklist>`, around its `<task-list-task>`s.

a "checklist" is a viewable list of tasks:
	// What it shows:  every task, the ones still to do, or the ones done
	- its "showing" is one of all, active or done
		- it "is showing (showing)"

	// on the page, its tasks can be dragged to another place:  they move as the pointer does, gliding there
	- its items can be reordered immediately
	// a drop has moved its tasks:  each keeps its new place
	- when a task is dropped on it:
		keep the order
	// each task, unless the filter hides it
	- to draw each item:
		if it is showing active and the task is done return nothing
		if it is showing done and the task is active return nothing
		return draw the task
	// Its tasks one under the other;  while it's empty, a line saying so
	- to draw it:
		<ui-stack spacing="xs">
			<if it is empty>
				<ui-text color="grey">Nothing to do</ui-text>
			</if>
			<children/>
		</ui-stack>
	// Each task keeps its place in the list, from 1, where it's kept:  so the order people drag them into comes back next time
	- to keep the order:
		for task, place in it
			set the order of task to place

	- to test the filter:
		set the tasks to a new checklist
		add (a new task with title = "a", done = yes) to the tasks
		add (a new task with title = "b") to the tasks
		the length of (tasks in the tasks where it is active) should be 1
	- to test a dragged order is kept:
		set the tasks to a new checklist
		set the first to a new task with title = "first"
		set the second to a new task with title = "second"
		add the second to the tasks
		add the first to the tasks
		keep the order of the tasks
		the order of the second should be 1
		the order of the first should be 2
		the title of the first task in (the tasks sorted by its order) should be "second"
// a task is in one checklist at a time
a task belongs to one checklist

## The app
// Its toolbar, the new task's field, then the list beside the property editor.

task list is an app:
	- its "checklist" is a new checklist
	// The next task's title, as the new task's field holds it
	- its "draft" is text
	- its "active count" is the length of (tasks in the checklist where it is active)

	// Where the tasks are kept:  the person picks, and the app asks that keeper
	- group "keeping"
	// Where the tasks are kept:  this browser, a JSON file on the server, a CSV file on the server, or your atmosphere account
	- its "storage" is one of browser, server, csv or atmosphere
	// Who keeps them, for where they're kept:  one of the keepers in the API files
	- its "keeper" is a task keeper

	- when its storage changes:
		if the storage is server
			set the keeper to a new server keeper
		otherwise if the storage is csv
			set the keeper to a new sheet keeper
		otherwise if the storage is atmosphere
			set the keeper to a new sky keeper
		otherwise
			set the keeper to a new browser keeper
		fill the checklist

	// The keeper's tasks, in the list;  a keeper with none starts with a few
	- to fill the checklist:
		clear the checklist
		for task in (the kept tasks of the keeper) sorted by its order
			add it to the checklist
		if the checklist is not empty return
		add the starting task "Write the Task List example" with priority high
		add the starting task "Teach it to draw" with priority normal
		add the starting task "Select some tasks, then edit them together" with priority normal
		add the starting task "Drag tasks to reorder them" with priority low
		set the done of the first task in the checklist to yes

	// A new task list keeps its tasks in this browser, and shows every one
	- to create it:
		set the showing of the checklist to all
		set the storage to browser
		set the keeper to a new browser keeper
		fill the checklist

	- to add the starting task (title as text) with priority (level as text):
		set task to keep a new task titled title of the keeper
		set the priority of task to level
		add task to the checklist
		set the order of task to the length of the checklist

	// The draft, as a new task at the end of the list;  the field empties
	- to add the draft:
		if the draft is "" return
		set title to the draft
		set task to keep a new task titled title of the keeper
		set the priority of task to normal
		add task to the checklist
		set the order of task to the length of the checklist
		clear the draft

	// Which tasks the list shows:  the toolbar ticks the one it's showing
	- group "filter"
	- to show all:
		- titled "All"
		- icon "list"
		- selected when the checklist is showing all
		set the showing of the checklist to all
	- to show to do:
		- titled "To do"
		- icon "square outline"
		- selected when the checklist is showing active
		set the showing of the checklist to active
	- to show done:
		- titled "Done"
		- icon "check square outline"
		- selected when the checklist is showing done
		set the showing of the checklist to done
	- to remove the done tasks:
		- titled "Remove the done tasks"
		- icon "trash alternate outline"
		for task in (tasks in the checklist where it is done)
			throw the task away
			remove the task from the checklist

	// The toolbar's buttons, and the list's right click:  the same actions
	- group "menus"
	- its "tasks menu" is a menu of "show all" , "show to do" , "show done" , "-" and "remove the done tasks"
	- its "show menu" is a menu of "show all" , "show to do" and "show done" titled "Show"
	// A right click on the list:  which tasks it shows, as a menu of its own, then tidying up
	- its "list menu" is a menu of "show menu" , "-" and "remove the done tasks"

	// The property editor edits every selected task at once:  a property they disagree on shows Mixed
	- to draw it:
		<ui-container>
			<ui-stack>
				<ui-toolbar menu="tasks menu" aria-label="Tasks">
					<ui-text slot="title" size="large">Task List</ui-text>
					<ui-text slot="right">
						<if the active count is 0>All done<otherwise>{the active count} to do</otherwise>
					</ui-text>
				</ui-toolbar>
				<ui-form value={it}>
					<ui-stack>
						<ui-field label="Keep them in" inline>
							<ui-select name="storage">
								<ui-item value="browser" icon="desktop">This browser</ui-item>
								<ui-item value="server" icon="server">A JSON file on the server</ui-item>
								<ui-item value="csv" icon="table">A CSV file on the server</ui-item>
								<ui-item value="atmosphere" icon="cloud">Your atmosphere account</ui-item>
							</ui-select>
						</ui-field>
						<ui-input name="draft" placeholder="Something to do" aria-label="New task" fluid action>
							<ui-button slot="action" color="primary" disabled={the draft is ""} onClick={add the draft}>Add</ui-button>
						</ui-input>
					</ui-stack>
				</ui-form>
				<ui-grid columns="2" stackable context-menu="list menu">
					{draw the checklist}
					<ui-property-editor label="Selected tasks" schema="task-list-task" value={the selection of the checklist}>
						<ui-property name="title"/>
						<ui-property name="priority"/>
						<ui-property name="done"/>
						<ui-property name="notes"/>
					</ui-property-editor>
				</ui-grid>
			</ui-stack>
		</ui-container>
